# Greensleeves, fingerstyle solo (repertoire plan: greensleeves-fingerstyle). A new arrangement
# of the anonymous Elizabethan tune: bass on each dotted-quarter beat (A for Am, G for G, E for E,
# C for C), the tune on top, chord notes filling in under long tune notes. The sixth note of the
# scale is F# throughout (the plan allows F or F#; it is kept the same everywhere).
title: Greensleeves (fingerstyle)
id: greensleeves-fingerstyle
composer: Traditional English
source: Anonymous tune registered in 1580; new solo arrangement for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: fingerstyle, solo, 6/8, minor key
tempo: 81
time: 6/8
key: A minor
